Dataset content
---------------
Lapsus labels, corruptions and annotations are released under Apache-2.0.
The sentences themselves keep the licence of their source, recorded per row
in the `license` column and summarised in ATTRIBUTION.md, which is generated
by `python -m lapsus build` and shipped with every release and Hub mirror.

* Tatoeba (https://tatoeba.org): sentences by the Tatoeba contributors,
  CC BY 2.0 FR unless released as CC0 1.0.

Test fixtures
-------------
tests/fixtures/morphit_subset.txt is a small subset of the Morph-it! lexicon
(Marco Baroni and Eros Zanchetta, https://docs.sslmit.unibo.it/doku.php?id=resources:morph-it),
dual licensed CC BY-SA 2.0 and LGPL. It is used only by the offline tests and
keeps that licence. tests/fixtures/parses_*.json contain Stanza analyses of
sentences written by the Lapsus authors.

Tools used at build time (not redistributed)
--------------------------------------------
Stanza (Apache-2.0; Italian models trained on non-commercial treebanks),
LanguageTool (LGPL-2.1-or-later), Morph-it! (CC BY-SA 2.0 / LGPL),
LemmInflect (MIT), lingua-language-detector (Apache-2.0), datasketch (MIT),
openai-community/gpt2 (MIT), Qwen/Qwen2.5-0.5B (Apache-2.0).
